WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:05.400
Module 05 · Course 2 · Organise · For entrepreneurs
Internal Systems & Operations

2
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.800
Choose the minimum systems you need to start well for your work, money, people and information.

3
00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:30.985
This module helps you choose the minimum systems you need to start well: how work, money, people and information flow, which processes to write down, one planning calendar and simple tools. It answers: what must work reliably from the first day?

4
00:00:31.385 --> 00:00:31.985
Why systems matter early

5
00:00:31.985 --> 00:00:38.400
1. Simple routines set now save you from chaos once orders and people arrive.

6
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:44.444
2. Some protections, such as handling data and money, cannot wait until later.

7
00:00:44.444 --> 00:00:51.119
3. Written processes let more than one person do the work safely.

8
00:00:51.519 --> 00:01:01.669
What you will work through: 5.1 What a system is: your organisational operating map · 5.2 Minimum viable systems by stage · 5.3 Processes, SOPs and process ownership · 5.4 The planning and reporting calendar · 5.5 People and HR systems overview · 5.6 Finance, procurement and internal controls overview · 5.7 Compliance essentials from day one · 5.8 Information, documents and knowledge management · 5.9 Digital tools and the tech stack · 5.10 Issues, actions and decisions tracking · 5.11 Recap: Internal Systems & Operations

9
00:01:02.069 --> 00:01:02.669
What you will have

10
00:01:02.669 --> 00:01:08.713
1. An operating map showing how your work, money, people and information connect.

11
00:01:08.713 --> 00:01:14.757
2. A minimum set of systems, with clear triggers for adding the next.

12
00:01:14.757 --> 00:01:22.172
3. Key processes written down, one planning calendar and a simple set of tools.

13
00:01:22.572 --> 00:01:23.172
Keep it light

14
00:01:23.172 --> 00:01:30.328
1. Write the process before choosing any app; a phone and shared drive may be enough.

15
00:01:30.328 --> 00:01:36.743
2. Decide where files live and how they are named before they pile up.

16
00:01:36.743 --> 00:01:44.157
3. Use our example bakery’s routines for orders, stock and cash as a model.

17
00:01:44.757 --> 00:01:46.757
You create: Your Internal Systems Blueprint: an operating map, minimum systems, processes, calendar and tools.

18
00:01:46.757 --> 00:01:51.557
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

19
00:01:53.057 --> 00:01:56.157
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
